Greetings,

after "Bit Prepared: a missing link?"
(http://www.linuxjournal.com/article.php?sid=7533)

I am happy to announce "Bit Prepared II: Richard Stallman Meets the
World Scout Bureau" (http://www.linuxjournal.com/article.php?sid=7813)

where "Richard Stallman from the FSF, Ray Saunders from the World
Scout Bureau and the author discuss the connections between free
software and Scouting philosophies"

Miscellanea:

1) To contact me directly, please only use the address
   mentioned in the URL above.
2) If you know somebody who can translate it in other
   languages, possibly before the Jamboree on the Internet,
   please contact me.
3) I will try to follow all the newsgroup, but will mainly
   check the forum associated to the article. I am much more
   likely to give public answers there than anywhere else,
   simply for lack of time
4) Please keep me informed off list of any development
   in your area/troop about usage of Free Software.

Thanks for your attention,

Marco Fioretti

