Dear all,
It is my pleasure to announce that lina version 4.0.5 has been released.
 You can download via
    http://home.hccnet.nl/a.w.m.van.der.horst/lina.html

ABOUT LINA:
lina is the Linux version of ciforth(computer intelligence/common Intel
Forth), an interpreter environment, scripter and compiler for Forth.
It is (large and by) compliant with the ISO Forth standard; the
CODE wordset is fully implemented. The small, classic,
indirect threaded kernel contains the essential, i.a. file access and
exceptions. Its power is multiplied by an extensive source library,
that add i.a. a decompiler and integrated 386 assembler.
It comes with a comprehensive 150 page manual (for a 30kbyte =
executable!).

CHANGES:
Since the original annoucement lina has been used for substantial =
projects
(rebuild of manx, regular expression filtering, the reverse engineering =
tool
computer_intelligence_assembler_disassembler_386).
Few bugs have been found. Changes are mostly improvements in the
documentation and additions to the library.
Additions to the library:
- struct endstruct : a tool for building structures-with-methods
- bags : handles sets and bags
Bugs:
- !CSP reverted to original fig-forth compatibility
- SEARCH-WORDLIST happened to be the ISO-word CURRENT (now renamed)

Note: a compatible tool voor MS-Windows platforms is available via
Simtel.

Albert van der Horst,Oranjestr 8,3511 RA UTRECHT,THE NETHERLANDS
        One man-hour to invent,
                One man-week to implement,
                        One lawyer-year to patent.
albert@spenarnc.xs4all.nl http://home.hccnet.nl/a.w.m.van.der.horst
