From: "Niraj Sahay" <niraj@efyindia.com>
Subject: LINUXFor You


[Commercial]

Dear Linux enthusiasts,

LINUXForYou: The Complete Magazine on Open Source.
LINUXForYou's October issue is now on stands, it has a lot
of content which the community would like to get their
hands on.

October's Focus
LINUXForYou: Munich has now become a Linux city.
LINUXForYouPRO: PHP's creator Rasmus Lerdorf shares his
thoughts on the PHP phenomenon with LFY's readers.

Other highlights of the October issue includes:
----------------------------------------------------------
LFY CD #1

This time CD #1 is bundled with the following software
*Compiere: Compiere is an enterprise resource planning cum
customer relationship management tool. It is a smart
solution for all business management needs.

*Magic Point: With Magic Point software you can create
presentations with your favourite text editors.

*MEPIS Linux: This Linux is termed as Linux for SOHOs. It
can be automatically optimised and customised for any
application and need. This software is newbie-friendly
software.

LFY CD #2

Knoppix 3.6 distro: A complete version of Knoppix 3.6 is
available on this CD. This is a distro of its kind, you
name an application and it's done.

LINUX For You
--------------------
Articles in detail

*Munich: The Linux City: Munich in Germany has become a
Linux city. The city has migrated from Windows to Linux.
Read this story to know how this migration carried out.

*Industry survey: Linux in Telecommunication: This survey
marks the presence of Linux in the telecommunication
sector. According to this survey, there is 100 per cent
awareness of Linux in the industry.

*Fall in the prices of Linux laptops: This article shows
how Linux has forced laptop manufacturers to cut down
their prices. You can check out branded laptops for as low
as Rs 29, 999. So take your pick now.


LINUX For You PRO
-------------------------
Articles in detail

*Do You PHP?: This article presents an overview of the PHP
phenomenon, what has shaped and motivated the language and
where it is heading now.

*Troubleshooting software: This article describes the
basic tools you need to manage software packages in the
RPM format in Fedora and Red Hat Linux systems.

*Installing Compiere: This article presents a step by step
guide for installing Compiere on your desktop. Compiere is
an ERP-cum-CRM software for small and medium sized
business enterprises.

*Review: Knoppix 3.6: In this article, Knoppix 3.6 has
been reviewed in detail.


Why do we have two versions of Linux For You now?
------------------------------------------------------------------
Linux For You was conceived with the aim of pushing Linux
from labs to offices. To achieve this goal, we realised
that we needed to reduce the pricing of the main magazine
so that those who were not technical but curious about
Linux/OSS could access the information. Hence,
LINUXForYou's main magazine was created as a magazine for
everyone to read.

At the same time, the demand from the tech community was
clear -- they needed technical content along with CDs that
bundled the latest software and distros. Hence, the
combined pack of LINUXForYou and LFYPRO and the two CDs is
now available at Rs 100!

For more details about LINUX For You magazine, log on to
www.linuxforu.com or email at niraj@efyindia.com.

This communication aims to inform the Linux community
about the information contained in Asia's only magazine on
Linux and open source, and we hope that it will be taken
positively.

